    <dcterms:title>Phineas Finn
The Irish Member</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phineas_Finn</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>E-text prepared by Joseph E. Loewenstein, M.D.</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Phineas Finn" by Anthony Trollope is a novel first published serially from 1867 to 1868. It follows a charming young Irishman who enters British Parliament with no salary and little fortune. To survive in London's political world, Phineas must navigate party politics, contentious reforms, and his romantic entanglements with several women of wealth. His friendships, ambitions, and heart pull him between loyalty and opportunity, forcing difficult choices that will determine both his political career and personal future. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 80.6 (6th grade). Easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
